From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: armada-os/armada#748 reporter <noreply@github.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ir3/array_to_ssa: follow trivial phi chains in lookup_value

A trivial phi's data can point at another phi that is itself removed
later, so returning it straight away hands out a definition that no
longer exists. The shader compiler then crashed on some games' shaders
at startup (Enshrouded, Onimusha: Way of the Sword). Follow the chain
to the final definition instead.

The reporter's fix from armada-os/armada#748, carried there until
mesa#16676 is resolved upstream.
---
diff --git a/src/freedreno/ir3/ir3_array_to_ssa.c b/src/freedreno/ir3/ir3_array_to_ssa.c
index dacd516d..896bee97 100644
--- a/src/freedreno/ir3/ir3_array_to_ssa.c
+++ b/src/freedreno/ir3/ir3_array_to_ssa.c
@@ -161,10 +161,14 @@ remove_trivial_phi(struct ir3_instruction *phi)
 static struct ir3_register *
 lookup_value(struct ir3_register *reg)
 {
-   if (!reg)
-      return NULL;
-   if (reg->instr->opc == OPC_META_PHI)
-      return reg->instr->data;
+   /* A trivial phi's data can be another phi that is removed later, so
+    * follow the chain to the final definition. */
+   while (reg && reg->instr->opc == OPC_META_PHI) {
+      struct ir3_register *next = reg->instr->data;
+      if (next == reg)
+         break;
+      reg = next;
+   }
    return reg;
 }
 
